# Every path outside the course tree that install-cs193v.sh changes on a machine whose only
# missing piece is a subuid range. Read this list; it is the blast radius of a real install.
#
#   /etc/subuid, /etc/subgid   what the installer set out to change
#   /etc/subuid-, /etc/subgid- usermod's own backups of them
#   /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow   usermod rewrites the whole shadow suite, not just the ranges
#   /etc/.pwd.lock             its lock file
#   /work                      the read-only mount this harness adds, not the installer
#   the bare directories       mtimes, from writing the files above
#
# Lines beginning # are comments. Anything appearing in `podman diff` and NOT here fails the
# run, and anything here that stops appearing fails it too -- so this is a claim in both
# directions rather than a filter that quietly grows.
A /work
C /etc
C /etc/.pwd.lock
C /etc/passwd
C /etc/shadow
C /etc/subgid
C /etc/subgid-
C /etc/subuid
C /etc/subuid-
C /home
C /home/student
C /tmp
